# wlink directive -- 3com-pktdrv (fully-assembly floor).
#
# One NASM object, DOS MZ .EXE, no C library. Entry point is ..start (carried in the OMF
# module-end record by NASM). The resident region (resident_image + state in _BSS) is
# packed by copy-down at runtime; class ordering for a tight TSR keep-boundary returns when
# the install + DOS-keep path lands.

system dos
name build/3cpd.exe
option quiet
option map=build/3cpd.map
# DOSSEG order: CODE first, then DATA, with _BSS + _STACK last so the uninitialized
# regions fall under minalloc instead of being stored in the file image.
option dosseg

file build/start.obj
